  "topic_en": "Gauss derives theta-function identities (series in squares of exponents) expressed as infinite products with factors (1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^15)..., combining them by addition and factorizing via the Jacobi triple product.",
  "transcription": "Da nun $\\frac{x(1-x^3)(1-x^{15})(1-x^{27})(1-x^{39})\\ldots[x^{18}]}{x(1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})(1-x^{21})\\ldots} = \\frac{[x^{18}]^2}{[x^9]} = 1+x^9+x^{27}+x^{54}+\\&c.$ so ist\n[27] $x-x^9-x^{16}+x^{25}+x^{49}\\ldots = (1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\ldots\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}}\\left\\{x^{\\frac{9}{8}}+x^{\\frac{81}{8}}+x^{\\frac{225}{8}}+x^{\\frac{441}{8}}+\\&c.\\right\\}$\nFerner folgt aus 24, wenn man statt x, $x^3$ setzt, und\n[28] $\\frac{1-2x^9+2x^{36}-2x^{81}+}{(1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\ldots} = \\frac{[x^6][x^{9}]^2}{[x^3][x^{18}]} = 1+x^3+x^6+x^{15}+x^{21}+\\&c.$\n[28] $1-2x^9+2x^{36}-2x^{81}+\\&c. = (1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\ldots\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}}\\left\\{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}+x^{\\frac{25}{8}}+x^{\\frac{49}{8}}+\\&c.\\right\\}$\nAlso aus der Verbindung von 27 u. 28\n[29] $1-2x+2x^4-2x^9+2x^{16}-\\&c. = (1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\ldots\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}}\\left\\{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}-2x^{\\frac{9}{8}}+x^{\\frac{25}{8}}+x^{\\frac{49}{8}}-2x^{\\frac{81}{8}}\\ \\&c.\\right\\}$\nFerner folgt aus 23\n$x^{\\frac{1}{8}}-x^{\\frac{25}{8}}-x^{\\frac{49}{8}}+x^{\\frac{121}{8}}+\\&c. = x^{\\frac{1}{8}}[x^3]$ also\n[30] $1-2x^3+2x^{12}-2x^{27}+2x^{48}-\\&c. = (1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\ldots\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}}\\left\\{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}-x^{\\frac{25}{8}}-x^{\\frac{49}{8}}+x^{\\frac{121}{8}}+x^{\\frac{169}{8}}-\\&c.\\right\\}$\nAus der Summation von 29 u. 30\n[31] $\\{1-2x+2x^4-2x^9\\}+\\{1-2x^3+2x^{12}-2x^{27}+\\&c\\} = (1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\ldots\\frac{2}{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}}\\left\\{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}-x^{\\frac{9}{8}}-x^{\\frac{81}{8}}+x^{\\frac{121}{8}}+x^{\\frac{169}{8}}-\\&c.\\right\\}$\nAus der Summation von 28 u. 30\n[32] $\\{1-2x^3+2x^{12}-2x^{27}+\\}+\\{1-2x^9+2x^{36}-2x^{81}+\\} = (1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\ldots\\frac{2}{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}}\\left\\{x^{\\frac{1}{8}}+x^{\\frac{49}{8}}+x^{\\frac{169}{8}}+x^{\\frac{529}{8}}+\\right\\}$\nSetzt man in 6 statt x, $x^6$ u. statt y, xy so wird\n$(1+x^7y)(1+x^{19}y)(1+x^{31}y)\\ldots(1+\\frac{x^5}{y})(1+\\frac{x^{17}}{y})\\ldots[x^{12}] = (1+\\frac{x^5}{y}+x^7y+\\frac{x^{22}}{yy}+x^{26}yy\\ldots)$\nMan hat demnach die Zerlegungen in factoren\n[33] $\\{1-2x^3+2x^{12}-2x^{27}\\}+\\{1-2x^9+2x^{36}-2x^{81}+\\} = 2[x^{36}](1-x^3)(1-x^9)(1-x^{15})\\ldots(1+x^{15})(1+x^{21})(1+x^{51})(1+x^{57})\\ldots$\n[34] $\\{1-2x+2x^4-2x^9\\}+\\{1-2x^3+2x^{12}-2x^{27}\\} = 2[x^{12}]\\{(1-x)(1-x^3)(1-x^5)(1-x^7)\\ldots(1+x^5)(1+x^7)(1+x^{17})(1+x^{19})\\ldots$\n[35] $\\{1+2x^3+2x^{12}+2x^{27}\\}+\\{1+2x^9+2x^{36}+2x^{81}\\} = 2[x^{36}]\\{(1+x^3)(1+x^9)(1+x^{15})\\ldots(1-x^{15})(1-x^{21})(1-x^{51})\\ldots$\n[36] $\\{1+2x+2x^4+2x^9\\}+\\{1+2x^3+2x^{12}+2x^{27}\\} = 2[x^{12}]\\{(1+x)(1+x^3)(1+x^5)\\ldots(1-x^5)(1-x^7)(1-x^{17})\\ldots$\nHieraus ergeben sich zugleich die Factoren des letzten Theils in 31",
